{
  "id": "COMPOUND:26277 - PROTEIN:6153",
  "verbalization": "Stecholide I is shown to interact with CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which is a target of multiple compounds, including Leosibirone B and (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan. All these compounds are implicated in the target of Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like. This suggests a potential mechanism where Stecholide I may inhibit Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like through a shared pathway involving sialyltransferase activity. The evidence is consistent with a mechanism where Stecholide I acts as a competitive inhibitor of the sialyltransferase, which in turn may affect the activity of Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like. The final scores indicate a plausible relationship, but further validation is needed to confirm the exact mode of action and the biological relevance of this interaction.",
